      "math_academy_id": "q-130950",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $4$th and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns.",
